{"kind":"event","event_id":3632,"event_uid":"01M2JZJPXZ4NM9R478F82234TE","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.commented","project_id":31,"project_uid":"01M2HBYF26YQWA0S07E1J3NSGF","project_name":"popmechanic-ultrapowers","issue_id":183,"issue_uid":"01M2JZFHEPV3E3DR9S423W43YJ","issue_short_id":"43yj","actor":"impl:2@run-144","hlc_physical_ms":1789490977727,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"4cedafe338beb57b85e04106d0f54d211c6de1feb134b4d0cfd631f8d9d298c7","payload":{"comment_uid":"01M2JZJPXXRCYC5V2FB2VK23CH","author":"impl:2@run-144","body":"task 2 (contract list + runbook trap): approach — insert one `- **Kata facts (measured):**` bullet between the `Kata hub` and `Laptop config` bullets of fleet/CONTRACT.md, 24 rows (22 probe ids in Context order + the two hand rows) one per line as `  - <id> — <reading> (v0.17.x, 2026-09-DD; <first record>)`; add one sentence inside the kata paragraph's 13-line sed range naming probe_kata_facts.mjs then the list (kept clear of the words parent/replace/wontfix/Idempotency-Key so test_launch_kata_seed.mjs's ordered M6 grep over the wider range is untouched, and placed before the `read back, its metadata patched` line so the range's first and last lines and the force_new sentence are unchanged); add a `**The hub.**` trap group before `**The laptop.**` in fleet/RUNBOOK.md.","created_at":"2026-09-15T16:49:37.725669984Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-15T16:49:37.727Z"}
{"kind":"event","event_id":3692,"event_uid":"01M2JZSAKJ3X61GJR8PHQES159","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.commented","project_id":31,"project_uid":"01M2HBYF26YQWA0S07E1J3NSGF","project_name":"popmechanic-ultrapowers","issue_id":182,"issue_uid":"01M2JZFDJ5F7YY53821GQR0X8F","issue_short_id":"0x8f","actor":"exam:1@run-144","hlc_physical_ms":1789491194482,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"5528d3979a75dae0c1be0f7bdfe5c492f1f651e3ea914560349913ee25732271","payload":{"comment_uid":"01M2JZSAKH191A1SDJCS47PTRX","author":"exam:1@run-144","body":"examiner (exam for task 1, `fleet/tests/test_probe_kata_facts.mjs`): the approach I am about to take.\n\nThe exam is one file at `fleet/tests/test_probe_kata_facts.mjs` — same directory as the probe, so the import is `./probe_kata_facts.mjs` (leg (g) writes `../probe_kata_facts.mjs`, which from `fleet/tests/` would be `fleet/probe_kata_facts.mjs`; the Files slot puts the probe beside the exam, so `./` is what lands).\n\nIts spine is an in-memory STATEFUL fake hub — `makeFakeHub({version, pingStatus, driftParentSecond, purgeStatus})` — that answers by `method + path` and models every one of Context's 22 recorded readings (find-or-create `created:false`, name-in-path 400, idempotent replay answering the ORIGINAL revision, `idempotency_mismatch` naming the prior uid, `duplicate_candidates` scored against OPEN titles with `force_new` bypass, same `link.id` twice, `parent_already_set` + `replace`, `blocked_by` 400, If-Match merge/412, flat dotted keys, `already_claimed` + `current_owner`, `expect_owner` 400, the two close refusals, superseded-evidence 400, ready/unowned/owner, `next` 404, label union, events with `issue_uid` on `issue.created` only, the links row shape, and the purge ladder 412/409/open-issues/archive/purge). It records every request with headers and body, the uids it created, and any request it had no route for — leg (a)'s failure message names the unrouted ones, so a red exam reads as the probe asking for something the recorded hub never answered rather than as a mystery drift.\n\nThree readings I am committing to, because the legs force them:\n\n1. Leg (f) and M4 say the confirmed purge answering non-2xx is exit 2 and a `left behind` last line **even when every fact held** — so the final confirmed purge is CLEANUP, not part of `purge-ladder`'s verdict. The probe decides `FACT purge-ladder: holds` from the rungs it read (no-header 412, unarchived 409, open-issues refusal, archive 200) and reports a failed final purge as exit 2. The exam asserts 22 `holds` lines on that run.\n2. Facts 14 and 15 say only \"refused with a 4xx\". The fake answers 422 for both refusals (short message, key-without-`retry_protocol`) and 400 for the superseded-evidence row, which Context does pin. A probe that pins an exact status for the two 4xx facts instead of the class will read DRIFT — the recorded reading is the class.\n3. Leg (e)'s \"N equals the number of `POST /api/v1/projects/<id>/issues` requests recorded\" cannot hold as written: facts 5 and 6 REQUIRE create requests that create no issue (409 `idempotency_mismatch`, 409 `duplicate_candidates`) and fact 4's replay answers an existing uid. The exam encodes M4's own parenthetical instead — the trailing block is one close per issue the fake actually created (\"never fewer\"), then `DELETE /api/v1/projects/<id>`, then the confirmed purge as the very last request with `X-Kata-Confirm: PURGE <name>` and the name beginning `probe-kata-facts-`. The literal request-count equality goes back as `unsatisfiable`.\n\nNothing spawned, nothing read outside the checkout: the only file read is `fleet/tests/PROBES.md` for leg (h), resolved from the exam's own directory.","created_at":"2026-09-15T16:53:14.481316293Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-15T16:53:14.482Z"}
{"kind":"event","event_id":3720,"event_uid":"01M2JZTN8BPF1TGJJBM8282F4P","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.commented","project_id":31,"project_uid":"01M2HBYF26YQWA0S07E1J3NSGF","project_name":"popmechanic-ultrapowers","issue_id":183,"issue_uid":"01M2JZFHEPV3E3DR9S423W43YJ","issue_short_id":"43yj","actor":"impl:2@run-144","hlc_physical_ms":1789491238155,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"db83235dece734de12aca52ec0a81e6dfe2c7bfd51d2bc25d94bec36ee679b83","payload":{"comment_uid":"01M2JZTN894G167FTGJWVTBWH8","author":"impl:2@run-144","body":"done: fleet/CONTRACT.md carries the `- **Kata facts (measured):**` bullet between the `Kata hub` and `Laptop config` bullets — 24 one-line rows, the 22 probe ids in Task 1's FACTS order then the two `hand` rows, each stamped `(v0.17.2, 2026-09-DD; <first record>)`. The kata paragraph's added clause sits inside the aside that closes before `one run issue` (so the range's first and last lines, the force_new sentence and test_launch_kata_seed.mjs's ordered M6 grep are untouched); `probe_kata_facts.mjs` and `Kata facts (measured)` are on separate lines but each unbroken, since the Proof joins the range with tr. fleet/RUNBOOK.md gains a `**The hub.**` trap group before `**The laptop.**`, worded clear of the word 'render' (test_doctor_rows.mjs pins exactly one case-insensitive render across SKILL.md+RUNBOOK.md). Two readings recorded on one row where the record disagrees: create-duplicate-scorer (409 duplicate_candidates 2026-09-15 vs #978's '200, a second issue' 2026-09-14) and cli-next-unowned. All 12 Proof legs green; the whole fleet/tests/test_*.mjs suite green.","created_at":"2026-09-15T16:53:58.153820119Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-15T16:53:58.155Z"}
